WEBVTT

00:32:58.750 --> 00:33:01.875
either it becomes the ground
of a new enterprise

00:33:02.625 --> 00:33:05.726
into personal or otherwise.

00:33:05.750 --> 00:33:07.643
AG: So, OK. So --

00:33:07.667 --> 00:33:09.851
EP: You know, then of course,
you can go home

00:33:09.875 --> 00:33:12.559
and you can say to your wife
or to your partner,

00:33:12.583 --> 00:33:16.268
"I had a thought, I had a conversation
with this woman there, with her accent.

00:33:16.292 --> 00:33:18.601
And as I was thinking,
and I realized that --"

00:33:18.625 --> 00:33:22.184
And then she will say,
"Took you so long or something?"

00:33:22.208 --> 00:33:25.059
And look, either one values this ...

00:33:25.083 --> 00:33:28.059
It doesn't have
a monetary value necessarily.

00:33:28.083 --> 00:33:29.934
It has an existential value.

00:33:29.958 --> 00:33:32.226
I happen to think
that those things matter.